Decorator Purpose <code>@measure_duration</code> Sync duration histogram <code>@measure_duration</code> Async duration histogram <code>@count_calls</code> Sync call counter <code>@count_calls</code> Async call counter <pre><code>from archipy.helpers.decorators import count_calls, measure_duration


@measure_duration(attributes={"layer": "logic"})
@count_calls()
def process_payment(amount: float) -&gt; None:
    """Charge a payment amount.

    Args:
        amount: Amount to charge.
    """
    ...
</code></pre> <p>Instruments default to <code>{module}.{qualname}.duration</code> / <code>.calls</code> and record a <code>status</code> attribute (<code>ok</code> / <code>error</code> / <code>cancelled</code> for async cancel). Duration histograms use explicit second buckets and a description. <code>status</code> aligns with tracing: <code>BaseError</code> with HTTP status below 500 records as <code>ok</code> (handled client error), not <code>error</code>. A call that ends in <code>error</code> or <code>cancelled</code> also carries the standard <code>error.type</code> (the <code>BaseError.code</code>, or the fully qualified exception class); a call recorded as <code>ok</code> carries none. No-op when OTel or <code>METRICS_ENABLED</code> is off.</p>
